base=['Confirm adult first-line ES-SCLC (00908a), ECOG 0–2, adequate organ function, baseline ANC ≥1.5 and platelets ≥100 ×10⁹/L.','Baseline FBC, renal/liver profile, glucose and thyroid; current EMA SmPC additionally recommends amylase/lipase at treatment start and periodically. Measured isotope GFR preferred, or validated GFR/CrCl estimate; audiology as clinically indicated.','Review the current SmPC trial-population cautions (autoimmune history, active TB/hepatitis/HIV, recent live vaccine, pneumonitis/ILD history and significant cardiovascular disease); these are not automatically added NCCP contraindications.','Review untreated CNS metastases, symptomatic ILD, clinically significant infection and systemic immunosuppression >10 mg/day prednisolone equivalent (excluding topical/inhaled). Review previous anti-PD-1/PD-L1 treatment against current NCCP policy.','Check pregnancy/breastfeeding and component/excipient hypersensitivity. Exceptional mild carboplatin rechallenge needs immunology advice and controlled desensitisation.']
ongoing=['Disease monitoring and scans follow the supervising consultant’s treatment plan; the source does not impose the ASTRUM-005 research scan calendar.','Immune effects may appear after the final dose. Keep the patient alert card, urgent contacts and symptom vigilance; follow unresolved cytopenias, renal, liver or hormone abnormalities.','Current EMA SmPC adds amylase/lipase at baseline and periodically/as clinically indicated; assess affected organs more closely if immune toxicity occurs. Give an alert card with each prescription.','Lipid profile, ECG, cortisol and audiology are obtained as clinically indicated. Contraception for women of childbearing potential is required during serplulimab and at least six months after the last dose; reconcile all drug requirements.']
clinical_limits=['Serplulimab is not dose-reduced/escalated; use its own event-specific hold/stop/recovery rules. Withholding for tolerability is acceptable up to 12 weeks, not an automatic restart permission.','Counts and renal/hepatic rules apply to the relevant active component. Baseline ANC ≥1.5 differs from on-treatment ANC ≥1.0; the platelet 50–<75 source gap requires review.','Etoposide CrCl 10–50 suggests 75% original dose; bilirubin ≥50 µmol/L or decreased albumin suggests considering 50%. Reconcile simultaneous limitations and prior doses rather than multiplying fractions.','Serplulimab grade-4 endocrine table rows and the hormone-controlled footnote exception require specialist adjudication. Retreatment safety after immune myocarditis is unclear.','Grade 4 amylase/lipase laboratory elevation has a specific withhold row but conflicts with the general Grade 4 immune-event permanent-stop footnote; obtain consultant adjudication before restart.','NCCP etoposide renal standardisation uses CrCl10–50 for75% original dose, whereas product SmPC tables use15–50; reconcile product-specific dosing with pharmacy, particularly below15 or on dialysis.','Current EMA SmPC adds myasthenia Grade2 hold/Grades3–4 stop, SJS/TEN stop, acute thyroiditis and poorly controlled type1diabetes holds. These are labelled supplements to NCCP, not borrowed checkpoint-inhibitor rules.','An isolated high liver/creatinine value is not proof of immune toxicity. Confirm grade and attribution before a permanent-stop decision.']
